{
  "id": "E06",
  "title": "The Machine That Digs Without Bringing a City Down",
  "world": "strata",
  "fps": 30,
  "seed": "s02",
  "passages": [
    {
      "id": "P01",
      "text": "Above ground, a city keeps moving. Cars cross bridges. Trains arrive. People sleep in buildings that have stood for decades.",
      "estSec": 32.8,
      "flag": "",
      "words": 59
    },
    {
      "id": "P02",
      "text": "A tunnel boring machine, or TBM, is one of the most demanding tools in modern construction. India is using these machines on major rail projects. Large, specialised machines and their parts can involve complicated international supply chains.",
      "estSec": 20.6,
      "flag": "",
      "words": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "P03",
      "text": "This is not a story of one door slammed shut. It is a story of dependence on a few specialised machines, and the engineering needed to work underground.",
      "estSec": 15.6,
      "flag": "",
      "words": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "P04",
      "text": "Start with a spoon pushed into a bowl of wet sand. The spoon removes material, but the sand can collapse into the gap. Now imagine doing that beneath roads and buildings. Excavation is only half the problem. The other half is keeping the surrounding ground stable.",
      "estSec": 25.6,
      "flag": "",
      "words": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "P05",
      "text": "At the front of the machine is a rotating cutterhead. It breaks or scrapes away the material ahead. Behind it, systems carry the excavated material away. But a tunnel cannot be left as an unsupported hole. Depending on ground conditions and machine design, pressure at the excavation face must be carefully managed. On the Mumbai machines, pressurised slurry does that job.",
      "estSec": 33.9,
      "flag": "",
      "words": 61
    },
    {
      "id": "P06",
      "text": "Think of holding a hand against a door while someone pushes from the other side. If the opposing forces are badly balanced, the door moves. In tunnelling, the equivalent imbalance can allow the ground to shift. Engineers monitor pressure, movement and the behaviour of the soil or rock continuously.",
      "estSec": 27.2,
      "flag": "",
      "words": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "P07",
      "text": "Now look behind the cutterhead. As the machine advances, precast concrete segments can be assembled into rings. These rings become the tunnel lining. Imagine constructing the walls of a corridor immediately after carving out the space for it. The machine is not just digging a hole. It is helping create a supported passage.",
      "estSec": 29.4,
      "flag": "",
      "words": 53
    },
    {
      "id": "P08",
      "text": "In July twenty twenty-six, the railway ministry reported a second tunnel boring machine starting work. It is on the Mumbai to Ahmedabad bullet train line. Seven kilometres of that ten kilometre stretch run under Thane Creek. The scale is impressive. The more interesting fact is the coordination. Geology, machine control, surveying, segments, transport and safety all have to work together.",
      "estSec": 33.3,
      "flag": "",
      "words": 60
    },
    {
      "id": "P09",
      "text": "Here is a fictional scenario. A cutterhead encounters unexpectedly different ground. The machine cannot simply push harder without understanding the consequences. Operators adjust the excavation process, monitor movement and protect the ground above. Progress becomes a question of control, not brute force.",
      "estSec": 23.3,
      "flag": "FICTIONAL SCENARIO",
      "words": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "India's next challenge is deepening domestic capability in high-value machinery, specialised components, manufacturing, maintenance and engineering know-how.",
      "estSec": 18.3,
      "flag": "",
      "words": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "text": "The machine makes a tunnel. The industry behind the machine determines how easily the next tunnel can be built, repaired, adapted and completed.",
      "estSec": 16.7,
      "flag": "",
      "words": 30
    }
  ],
